        "summary": "🧬 ENDOGENOUS METABOLITE: 11-Hydroxy-Δ9-THC (11-OH-THC) is the primary psychoactive metabolite of cannabis (Δ9-THC), formed in the liver via CYP2C9 (~65%) and CYP3A4 (~25%) 11-hydroxylation before oxidation into inactive THC-COOH. Crossing the blood-brain barrier more rapidly than parent THC, 11-OH-THC is 1.5 to 2 times more potent at central CB1 cannabinoid receptors!\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Following oral cannabis ingestion (edibles), hepatic first-pass metabolism converts a massive fraction of THC into 11-OH-THC (≥1:1 ratio vs ~1:10 when smoked), explaining why edibles feel far more psychedelic, sedating, and last 6 to 12 hours.",
