        "summary": "4-CMC (4-chloromethcathinone or clephedrone) is a para-chlorinated synthetic cathinone. It displays higher serotonergic potency than 3-CMC, producing a warm empathogenic euphoria reminiscent of mephedrone (4-MMC). Like 3-CMC, its chlorinated structure carries severe concerns regarding serotonergic neurotoxicity similar to p-chloroamphetamine (4-CA).\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: More serotonergic and sedating than 3-CMC, delivering heavy entactogenic euphoria accompanied by pronounced neuronal and cardiovascular toxicity.",
        "effectsSummary": "Strong empathogenic euphoria, emotional openness, physical energy, pupillary dilation, nystagmus, jaw clenching (bruxism), and intense craving.",
        "dosageRemark": "Slightly more potent than 3-CMC. Insufflation is intensely painful and tissue-damaging. Oral ingestion in capsules or bombs is strongly recommended over sniffing.",
        "generalRisks": "Potential serotonergic neurotoxicity, serotonin syndrome risk, tachycardia, hyperthermia, dehydration, paranoia.",
        "longtermRisks": "Potential serotonergic axon damage, intense depressive comedowns, rapid psychological addiction.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Space sessions by several weeks (similar to MDMA/4-MMC)",
          "Never combine with other serotonergic substances",
          "Avoid insufflation to protect nasal septum and sinuses",
          "Pre-weigh and fix doses beforehand to prevent bingeing"
        ],
