        "summary": "An empathogen commonly used in place of MDMA, having a similar duration of empathogenic effects. This drug, however, has a longer stimulant \"tail,\" during which effects are more like those of amphetamines. Not to be confused with 4-FMA, which has a similar potency, but is not particularly empathogenic.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Compared to MDMA and speed, 4-FA features a unique biphasic profile: 2-3 hours of empathogenic, MDMA-like euphoria followed by several hours of clean amphetamine stimulation.",
        "effectsSummary": "Massive release of serotonin and dopamine, heightened empathy, deep feelings of interpersonal connection, tactile euphoria, and moderate physical stimulation.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Respect the 6 to 12 weeks spacing rule between sessions to allow complete serotonin replenishment.",
          "Stay hydrated reasonably (~250-500 ml water/electrolytes per hour during exertion to avoid hyponatremia).",
          "Never combine with antidepressants (SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs) due to lethal serotonin syndrome risk.",
          "Monitor body temperature closely and take frequent breaks in cool, ventilated areas."
        ],
