        "summary": "5-Hydroxytryptophan (commonly known as 5-HTP) is a naturally occurring amino acid and chemical precursor as well as a metabolic intermediate in the biosynthesis of the neurotransmitter serotonin. It is widely sold as an over-the-counter dietary supplement for depression, anxiety, insomnia, and mood enhancement. Combining 5-HTP with serotonergic substances such as MDMA or SSRIs carries a severe risk of serotonin syndrome.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Direct biochemical serotonin precursor, more effective and rapid than L-tryptophan for supporting sleep and mood without psychoactive stimulation.",
        "effectsSummary": "Subtle mood stabilization, mild anxiolysis, reduced sleep onset latency, and diminished emotional vulnerability during recovery periods.",
        "dosageRemark": "Standard supplemental dose: 50-200 mg taken in the evening. Begin with 50 mg with food to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort.",
        "generalRisks": "Nausea, gastrointestinal cramping, diarrhea, drowsiness, and headaches.",
        "longtermRisks": "Theoretical risk of cardiac valvular fibrosis with long-term high-dose use due to elevated peripheral blood serotonin levels.",
        "saferUse": [
          "NEVER take 5-HTP concurrently with SSRIs, SNRIs, MAOIs, or empathogens (MDMA, 3-MMC).",
          "Wait at least 24 hours after an MDMA experience before taking 5-HTP to aid recovery.",
          "Co-administer with green tea extract (EGCG) to inhibit peripheral decarboxylase and protect cardiac tissue."
        ],
        "crossTolerances": [],
        "toxicities": [],
        "isApproved": true,
        "url": "https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/5-Hydroxytryptophan"
