        "summary": "Acamprosate calcium (Aotal 333 mg, Campral) is a glutamatergic/NMDA modulator prescribed to maintain alcohol abstinence by calming post-withdrawal glutamatergic hyperexcitability and cravings. Not metabolized by the liver.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Non-sedative NMDA modulator stabilizing GABA/glutamate balance after alcohol cessation, carrying zero abuse potential and no noticeable acute high.",
