        "summary": "ALD-52, or N-acetyl-LSD is a less common chemical analogue of LSD, first synthesised by Albert Hoffman. It was famously implicated in the 'Orange Sunshine' trial. A psychedelic lysergamide, this compound exhibits similar properties to LSD, and is thought to be a pro-drug for LSD.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Compared to LSD, ALD-52 (1-acetyl-LSD) has a notably smoother, gentler onset with less initial come-up anxiety for an equivalent peak intensity.",
        "effectsSummary": "Intense sensory and visual alterations, altered perception of space and time, emotional amplification, deep introspection, and potential ego dissolution.",
