        "summary": "Alpha-GPC (L-alpha-glycerophosphocholine, choline alfoscerate) is a water-soluble nutrient which serves as a precursor to both choline and glycerophosphate within the brain. In humans, choline is considered to be an essential nutrient as its role in reducing the risk of neural tube defects, fatty liver disease, and other pathologies has been well-documented.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: High-bioavailability choline donor crossing the blood-brain barrier far more efficiently than choline bitartrate to boost acetylcholine and memory.",
