        "summary": "Amoxapine (N-desmethylloxapine, marketed as Defanyl or Asendin) is both the active N-demethylated metabolite of the antipsychotic loxapine (Loxapac) and a tetracyclic antidepressant. It combines potent norepinephrine transporter (NET) reuptake inhibition with 5-HT2A and dopamine D2 receptor antagonism (reinforced by its 7-hydroxyamoxapine derivative).\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Unique hybrid pharmacological profile bridging a noradrenergic antidepressant (like desipramine) and an atypical antipsychotic.",
