        "summary": "Buspirone (trade name Buspar among others) is an anxiolytic substance of the azapirone class. It is primarily used to treat anxiety disorders, particularly generalized anxiety disorder (GAD.) It is a serotonin 5-HT1A receptor partial agonist, increasing action at serotonin receptors in the brain.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Non-sedative 5-HT1A anxiolytic taking 2-3 weeks to build efficacy, completely free of physical dependence, tolerance, or benzodiazepine-like sedation.",
        "effectsSummary": "Central nervous system sedation, marked anxiolysis, muscle relaxation, psychomotor slowing, and reduction of inhibitions.",
        "dosageRemark": "STRICT 8-12h SCHEDULE: Taken 2 to 3 times daily consistently either always with food or always without food (food doubles bioavailability!). The 'Heavy' threshold (30 mg) is the maximum single unit intake (maximum 60 mg/24h divided). Full anxiolytic effect takes 2-4 weeks.",
