        "summary": "Cannabidiol (also known as CBD and Epidiolex®) is a naturally-occurring cannabinoid found in the cannabis plant. It is one of some 113 identified cannabinoids in cannabis plants, accounting for up to 40% of the plant's extract. It does not possess the same psychoactivity as tetrahydrocannabinol (THC), which is responsible for the euphoric and hallucinogenic aspects of cannabis, and is typically described as non-intoxicating.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Non-psychoactive cannabinoid delivering body relaxation and gentle anxiolysis without cognitive high, buffering against THC-induced anxiety.",
        "effectsSummary": "Mild somatic relaxation, reduced physiological anxiety, muscle loosening, anti-inflammatory relief, and improved sleep latency without cognitive impairment.",
        "dosageRemark": "Typical wellness oral doses: 20-50 mg. Clinical anti-epileptic protocols: 5-20 mg/kg/day under specialist care.",
        "generalRisks": "Mild drowsiness, dry mouth, reduced blood pressure, and gastrointestinal upset at elevated doses.",
        "longtermRisks": "Potent inhibition of cytochrome P450 enzymes (CYP3A4, CYP2C19), substantially elevating serum levels of co-prescribed anticonvulsants, blood thinners, and statins.",
