        "summary": "Cathinone (S-(-)-cathinone) is the principal naturally occurring psychoactive alkaloid found in the fresh leaves of the khat shrub (*Catha edulis*), indigenous to the Horn of Africa and Arabian Peninsula. It serves as the chemical progenitor for the entire synthetic cathinone family. It acts as an amphetamine-like releaser of dopamine and norepinephrine.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Natural alkaloid from khat, structurally akin to amphetamine with slightly lower potency and a shorter duration of stimulating action (2-4h).",
