        "summary": "Cetirizine (Zyrtec, Virlix) is a second-generation H1 antihistamine and the major active carboxylic acid metabolite of hydroxyzine (Atarax), formed at ~55% via alcohol dehydrogenase (ADH). Being zwitterionic and a P-glycoprotein substrate, it crosses the blood-brain barrier much less than parent hydroxyzine while sustaining 24-hour H1 receptor blockade. It is excreted ~70% unchanged via renal glomerular filtration (GFR) and OAT tubular secretion.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Far less sedating and devoid of anticholinergic effects compared to parent hydroxyzine, but directly dependent on renal clearance.",
        "effectsSummary": "Selective, prolonged peripheral H1 histamine receptor blockade, 24-hour anti-allergic coverage, and mild central sedation.",
