        "summary": "Desalkylflurazepam (widely sold as the Research Chemical norflurazepam) is the ultra-long-acting active metabolite (half-life 40 to 120 hours, ~74h average) of several prescription benzodiazepines (flurazepam, quazepam, fludiazepam, ethyl loflazepate) and is commonly used standalone as an RC for prolonged anxiolysis or tapering.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Roughly twice as potent by weight as diazepam (5 mg norflurazepam ≈ 10 mg diazepam), heavier in muscle relaxation and hypnosis, with a 3-to-6-day elimination tail.",
