        "summary": "🧬 ENDOGENOUS METABOLITE: Desmethylclomipramine (norclomipramine) is the major active metabolite of clomipramine (Anafranil), formed at ~60% via CYP2C19, CYP1A2, and CYP3A4 N-demethylation, and subsequently cleared via CYP2D6 hydroxylation. Whereas parent clomipramine is a potent serotonin (SERT) blocker, desmethylclomipramine is a potent norepinephrine transporter (NET) inhibitor whose longer half-life (~36h vs ~24h for parent) results in steady-state plasma levels 1.5 to 2.5 times higher than parent clomipramine.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Converts clomipramine into a dual potent SERT + NET tricyclic at steady state.",
