        "summary": "Desomorphine (also known as Dihydrodesoxymorphine) is an opioid substance of the morphinan chemical class that produces analgesic, muscle-relaxing, sedative, and euphoric effects when administered.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Fast-acting opioid 8 to 10 times more potent than morphine, notorious for devastating tissue necrosis in contaminated artisanal street forms (Krokodil).",
