        "summary": "Desoxypipradrol (also known as 2-DPMP) is a long-acting stimulant substance of the piperidine class. It acts as a potent dopamine and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor. Notable for its exceptionally long duration of action (often exceeding 24 to 48 hours), it carries a high risk of prolonged insomnia, acute anxiety, and stimulant psychosis with redosing.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Ultra-long-acting stimulant active at microgram/milligram doses (24-48h duration), carrying severe risks of protracted insomnia and sleep-deprivation psychosis.",
        "effectsSummary": "Unrelenting 24-48 hour wakefulness, continuous physical arousal, absolute suppression of fatigue, and severe sleep deprivation.",
        "dosageRemark": "⚠️ EXTREME 24-48 HOUR DURATION: Active at micro-doses (1-5 mg). NEVER REDOSE. Extremely high risk of sleep-deprivation psychosis.",
        "generalRisks": "Prolonged insomnia, severe paranoid delirium, visual hallucinations, cardiovascular strain, and panic.",
        "longtermRisks": "Severe psychiatric breaks, physical exhaustion, and potential self-harm under paranoid delusions.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Strongly advised to avoid this substance due to extreme duration.",
          "If consumed, keep doses under 2 mg, never redose, and keep rescue benzodiazepines/antipsychotics accessible."
        ],
