        "summary": "Desvenlafaxine (O-desmethylvenlafaxine, marketed as Pristiq) is the primary active metabolite of venlafaxine (Effexor), formed at ~65% in the liver via CYP2D6, as well as a standalone prescription SNRI antidepressant. Unlike parent venlafaxine, its clearance relies on phase II UGT conjugation and direct renal excretion (~45% unchanged), making its elimination independent of CYP2D6 polymorphisms.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Longer half-life than parent venlafaxine (11h vs 5h) and a stronger norepinephrine-to-serotonin reuptake ratio (~10:1 SERT:NET vs ~30:1 for venlafaxine).",
        "effectsSummary": "Dual serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake inhibition (SNRI), mood stabilization, generalized anxiety relief, and noradrenergic drive.",
