        "summary": "Dichloropane (also known as RTI-111 or O-401) is a novel stimulant substance of the phenyltropane class. Its effects include stimulation, thought acceleration, appetite suppression and euphoria.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Phenyltropane cocaine analog with a much longer duration of action (several hours) but flatter euphoria, providing steady dopaminergic stimulation.",
