        "summary": "Doxepin is a tricyclic antidepressant (TCA) acting as a serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor alongside strong antihistaminic, anticholinergic, and alpha-1 blocking properties. Tricyclic antidepressant and extremely potent H1 histamine antagonist (Quitaxon, Silenor); used at 3-10 mg for sleep-maintenance insomnia and 25-100+ mg for depression and anxiety.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Tricyclic antidepressant with exceptionally strong H1 antihistaminic affinity, highly effective for insomnia maintenance at low doses (3-6 mg).",
        "effectsSummary": "Antidepressant, neuropathic pain relief, and strong sedation/sleep induction; causes dry mouth, constipation, orthostatic dizziness, and blurred vision.",
