        "summary": "Ephylone (also known as N-ethylpentylone and bk-EBDP) is a synthetic cathinone substance with stimulant and entactogenic properties. It acts as a norepinephrine-dopamine reuptake inhibitor and serotonin releaser, producing stimulation, alertness, and euphoria, but has been linked to numerous emergency hospitalizations and fatal overdoses internationally.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Entactogenic cathinone delivering pleasant early empathy followed by protracted residual peripheral stimulation, insomnia, and tachycardia.",
