        "summary": "Eslicarbazepine (licarbazepine / 10-monohydroxy derivative MHD, marketed as Zebinix) is the active metabolite responsible for over 90% of the therapeutic effect of oxcarbazepine (Trileptal), rapidly formed via cytosolic hepatic reductases. It stabilizes voltage-gated sodium channels in the slow inactivated state and is cleared via renal filtration (~65%) and UGT2B7 glucuronidation (~35%) with a 10-11h half-life.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Unlike carbamazepine, it does not form a toxic 10,11-epoxide metabolite and causes far less CYP450 enzyme induction.",
