        "summary": "Ethylcathinone (also known as Ethylpropion, Ethcathinone, and commonly as ETH-CAT) is a stimulant substance of the cathinone chemical class that produces stimulating and focus enhancing effects when administered. It is structurally related to cathinone and methcathinone (MCAT), which broadly shares the effects profile of amphetamine or methylphenidate.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Ethylated cathinone analog producing clean functional wakefulness, markedly less potent and euphoric than classic 4-MMC.",
