        "summary": "Fenethylline (also known as phenethylline, fenetylline, amphetamin​oethyl​theophylline, amfetyline, or by brand names including Captagon, Biocapton and Fitton) is a stimulant substance of the amphetamine class. It is a codrug for amphetamine and theophylline.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Co-drug (Captagon) metabolizing into amphetamine and theophylline, delivering sharp psychomotor alertness with tempered blood pressure spikes.",
        "effectsSummary": "Extreme physical stamina, total abolition of hunger and sleepiness, rapid speech, heightened vigilance, and aggressive confidence.",
        "dosageRemark": "⚠️ ILLICIT COUNTERFEIT WARNING: Street 'Captagon' pills rarely contain authentic fenethylline, typically consisting of adulterated amphetamine, caffeine, and diphenhydramine mixtures.",
        "generalRisks": "Tachycardia, severe hypertension, hyperthermia, acute paranoia, and insomnia.",
        "longtermRisks": "Severe amphetamine dependence, toxic paranoid psychosis, physical wasting, and cardiovascular cardiomyopathy.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Reagent test street tablets before consumption.",
          "Maintain hydration and nutrition during extended wakefulness.",
          "Do not redose repeatedly over consecutive days."
        ],
