        "summary": "Gaboxadol (also known as THIP) is a synthetic derivative of the fly agaric compound muscimol. It acts as a selective, direct super-agonist of extrasynaptic GABAA receptors containing the delta subunit, producing distinct hypnotic, analgesic, and dissociative-like perceptual alterations without classical benzodiazepine tolerance.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Direct extrasynaptic GABA-A agonist promoting restorative deep sleep without disrupting REM stages, with hallucinogenic qualities at higher levels.",
        "effectsSummary": "Profound sleepiness, induction of restorative slow-wave sleep without morning hangover, dreamlike perceptual distortions, and bodily relaxation.",
        "dosageRemark": "Investigational sleep doses: 10-20 mg taken at bedtime. Doses above 25 mg trigger perceptual hallucinations.",
        "generalRisks": "Disorientation, dizziness, vivid nightmares, nausea, and morning grogginess at excessive doses.",
        "longtermRisks": "Phase III clinical trials were halted due to psychiatric adverse effects including hallucinations and complex sleep behaviors.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Take strictly while already in bed.",
          "Never combine with alcohol or other GABAergic sedatives."
        ],
        "crossTolerances": [],
        "toxicities": [],
        "isApproved": false,
        "url": "https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Gaboxadol"
