        "summary": "Galantamine (also known as Nivalin, Razadyne, Razadyne ER, Reminyl, and Lycoremine) is a water soluble, reversible, competitive acetylcholinesterase inhibitor that functions as a nootropic, oneirogen, and mild dissociative substance. It is well known and used widely as a dream potentiator. Along with its oneirogenic effects, it has stimulant and nootropic effects in low doses, and has mild dissociative effects in higher doses. It is an alkaloid that is obtained either synthetically, or from the bulbs and flowers of Galanthus caucasicus, Galanthus woronowii and related genera. It is also available in both a prescription form and as an over-the-counter supplement.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Acetylcholinesterase inhibitor used off-label as a premier oneirogen to induce vivid lucid dreams and boost cognitive recall.",
        "effectsSummary": "Profound intensification of dream vividness, spontaneous dream lucidity, enhanced memory consolidation, and sharp cognitive focus.",
        "dosageRemark": "Lucid dreaming protocol: 4-8 mg taken after 4-5 hours of natural sleep (Wake-Back-To-Bed / WBTB protocol). Do NOT take at bedtime due to severe sleep onset disruption.",
        "generalRisks": "Acute nausea, vomiting, stomach cramps, muscle twitching, bradycardia, and sleep paralysis.",
        "longtermRisks": "Rapid receptor desensitization if used frequently (limit to once or twice weekly maximum), and cardiac rhythm abnormalities in predisposed patients.",
        "saferUse": [
          "Take strictly following the WBTB method: sleep 4.5 hours, wake up, ingest 4 mg galantamine with a light sip of water, and return to bed 20 minutes later.",
          "Co-administer with a choline source (Alpha-GPC) to prevent cholinergic headaches.",
          "Space sessions by at least 3-4 days to prevent rapid tolerance."
        ],
