        "summary": "Lormetazepam is a prescription benzodiazepine acting as a positive allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors. Short-to-intermediate acting 3-hydroxy benzodiazepine hypnotic (Noctamide 1 mg, 2 mg) metabolized directly by glucuronidation (no active CYP metabolites), widely prescribed for insomnia. Approximate potency equivalence: ~1-1.5 mg Lormetazepam ≈ 10 mg Diazepam. Do not combine with other CNS depressants.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Potent hypnotic benzodiazepine (1-2 mg = 10 mg diazepam) with a 10-12h half-life, ensuring uninterrupted night-time sleep continuity.",
