        "summary": "Mefenamic acid is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID / AINS) used to treat pain, fever, and inflammation. Fenamate NSAID (Ponstyl) commonly prescribed for dysmenorrhea, pelvic pain, and moderate inflammatory pain. Strict dosing intervals must be respected, and two different NSAIDs must never be combined.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: NSAID uniquely effective for acute menstrual pain (dysmenorrhea) due to targeted suppression of uterine prostaglandin synthesis.",
