        "summary": "Metamizole (dipyrone / Novalgine) is a potent non-opioid pyrazolone analgesic, antipyretic, and spasmolytic used for severe acute pain, colic, and refractory high fever.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Powerful non-opioid analgesic and antispasmodic for visceral colic and refractory fever, restricted in many countries due to rare agranulocytosis risks.",
        "effectsSummary": "Strong pain relief, smooth muscle spasm relief, and fever reduction without opioid sedation or gastric ulceration typical of classic NSAIDs.",
        "dosageRemark": "STRICT INTERVAL: Wait at least 6 hours between two intakes. The 'Heavy' threshold (1000 mg) is the maximum single unit dose per intake. Maximum daily dose: 4000 mg/24h.",
