        "summary": "N-Methyl-N-isopropyltryptamine, a tryptamine analogue of DMT, a very uncommon drug with very few reports of human use. Described as 'more psychedelic than hallucinogenic' users report only mild visuals with some stimulation and cognitive effects. One of the more stable tryptamines.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Compared to DMT, MiPT favors auditory enhancement and bodily warmth with modest alterations to the visual field.",
