        "summary": "N-Ethylhexedrone (also known as hexen and NEH) is a synthetic stimulant substance of the cathinone class. It acts primarily as a dopamine-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, producing short-lived stimulation, elevated focus, and euphoria, accompanied by a strong urge to redose.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Short-acting stimulant cathinone delivering a sharp dopaminergic rush and alert focus, accompanied by intense compulsive redosing urges.",
