        "summary": "🧬 ENDOGENOUS METABOLITE: Noribogaine (12-hydroxyibogamine) is the major active metabolite of ibogaine, formed at ~85% in the liver via CYP2D6 O-demethylation. While ibogaine's acute oneiric phase lasts 12-24h (t½ ~7.5h), noribogaine exhibits a 28 to 49-hour elimination half-life (~36h average) and persists for 4 to 7 days. It acts as a serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SERT), κ- and µ-opioid modulator, and neurotrophic factor (GDNF/BDNF) inducer.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Less visionary and ataxic than parent ibogaine, it drives the multi-day anti-craving afterglow while maintaining cardiac hERG / QT prolongation.",
