        "summary": "🧬 ENDOGENOUS METABOLITE: Nortilidine is the essential active metabolite of tilidine (Valoron), formed at ~85% during intestinal and hepatic first-pass N-demethylation via CYP3A4 and CYP2C19. Whereas parent tilidine is virtually inactive, (1R,2S)-nortilidine exhibits 100-fold higher µ-opioid receptor affinity alongside dopamine transporter (DAT) inhibition, mediating tilidine's rapid analgesia and euphoria (half-life ~4.5h).\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: True active moiety of tilidine, subsequently cleared to inactive bisnortilidine via CYP3A4/CYP2C19.",
