        "summary": "A opioid analgesic which is the main active metabolite of Tramadol. Alone, it is a few times more potent than Tramadol and has additional affinity for δ and κ-opioid receptors. Has proven popular when sold, but these occasions have been rare due to patent rights.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Compared to regular Tramadol, O-DSMT is its direct active metabolite, roughly 4 times more potent on pure mu-opioid analgesia with deeper sedation, without serotonin reuptake inhibition, completely eliminating tramadol's seizure and serotonin syndrome risks.",
        "effectsSummary": "Potent analgesia, warm sedation, opioid euphoria, sense of deep contentment, pinpoint pupils, respiratory depression, and gastrointestinal slowing.",
