        "summary": "Oxiracetam is a racetam nootropic, having a hydroxyl group being the only difference between this and Piracetam. It used as a nootropic, namely for increased cognitive function. It is usually used two to three times a day. This substance is normally taken with Choline, can cause headaches without the addition of Choline.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Compared to Piracetam, oxiracetam is distinctly more stimulating psychomotor-wise, particularly benefiting mathematical logic and mental speed.",
