        "summary": "Paraxanthine (1,7-dimethylxanthine, marketed as the nootropic supplement Enfinity) is the overwhelmingly dominant active metabolite of caffeine in humans (~84% of caffeine is converted to paraxanthine via hepatic CYP1A2). An adenosine A1 and A2A receptor antagonist at least as potent as caffeine with a ~4.5h half-life, it sustains wakefulness for hours after coffee consumption.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Cleaner cognitive and dopaminergic wakefulness than parent caffeine, producing less jitteriness, less tachycardia, and fewer GI side effects (as it bypasses theophylline and theobromine formation).",
        "effectsSummary": "Clean mental wakefulness, enhanced vigilance and focus (A1/A2A antagonism), striatal dopaminergic support, and fatigue reduction.",
        "dosageRemark": "Formed at 84% from Caffeine; standalone nootropic dose: 100 to 200 mg.",
        "generalRisks": "Insomnia if taken late in the day, mild heart rate elevation at high doses.",
        "longtermRisks": "Moderate adenosinergic tolerance with high daily intake.",
