        "summary": "A phenylpiperidine opioid first synthesised by Otto Eisleb in 1939, better known by the names meperidine and pethidine. An analgesic, once widely prescribed it has since declined in usage due to the discovery of a toxic metabolite - norpethidine. Also reacts dangerously with many drugs.\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Fast-acting synthetic opioid roughly 10 times less potent than morphine, carrying seizure risks upon repeated use due to toxic norpethidine accumulation.",
        "effectsSummary": "Potent analgesia, warm sedation, opioid euphoria, sense of deep contentment, pinpoint pupils, respiratory depression, and gastrointestinal slowing.",
        "saferUse": [
          "LETHAL OVERDOSE RISK: Always keep naloxone (Narcan, Nyxoid) immediately accessible.",
          "NEVER combine with benzodiazepines, alcohol, pregabalin, or any CNS depressants.",
          "Never use alone, and test with fentanyl/nitazene test strips before use.",
          "Space doses strictly to prevent severe physical dependence and debilitating withdrawal."
        ],
