        "summary": "🧬 ENDOGENOUS METABOLITE: The MC5 metabolite (pentanoic acid derivative) is the primary active metabolite of tianeptine (Stablon), formed at ~45% via mitochondrial beta-oxidation of its side chain (independent of hepatic CYP450s). Like parent tianeptine, MC5 is a direct µ-opioid receptor agonist, but its elimination half-life is nearly 3 times longer (~7.2 hours vs ~2.5h for tianeptine) and it relies primarily on renal excretion (GFR).\n\n⚖️ Comparative profile: Explains why tianeptine's antidepressant action and background opioid occupancy persist for 12-18h even though the parent drug's acute peak lasts only 2-3h.",
